# Stock nozzle of the MK4 generation; the CORE One family ships CHT brass
# instead, so on your machines this is the aftermarket baseline.
name = Prusa Nozzle brass 0.4
vendor = prusa
tip = brass
diameter = 0.4
high_flow = 0
abrasive_ok = 0
preset_variant = 0.4
retract = 0.7
retract_speed = 45
default_layer_h = 0.2
default_width = 0.45
default_speed_external = 170
default_speed_perimeter = 170
default_speed_infill = 200
default_speed_travel = 350
claim_mvs_pla = 16
claim_mvs_petg = 20
claim_mvs_asa = 18
note = [sourced] Flow claims: E3D Nextruder nozzle datasheet (standard brass
note = table; PLA 220C / PETG 240C / ASA 260C), e3d-online.com/pages/
note = prusa-nextrduder-nozzle-datasheet (URL misspelling is theirs).
note = [independent] investegate.de XL bench (Sunlu PLA Meta, 200C):
note = underextrusion-free to 22, saturation ~24. High-speed-PLA-specific:
note = it neither validates nor refutes E3D's regular-PLA 16 (which
note = back-scales to ~13 at 200C by the ~1%/C rule) -- different melt.
note = [independent] MK4 forum click-ladder (Prusament PLA): click onset 18 /
note = 20 / 22 mm3/s at 220 / 230 / 240 C; PETG click 27-28 but a
note = quality-based ceiling near 17 -- click onset is an upper bound, not a
note = printable ceiling. Retract/speeds: bundle 2.5.5 printer + default
note = quality print presets (claims, not measurements).
